{
  "id": "m3l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "Listas",
    "en": "Lists"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Guardar muchos valores"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Una **lista** es una colección ordenada de valores, escrita entre corchetes y separada por comas. Puede contener números, textos o lo que quieras, y crecer o encoger."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "numeros = [10, 20, 30]",
          "print(numeros)",
          "print(len(numeros))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "[10, 20, 30]",
          "3"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Índices: acceder por posición"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Cada elemento tiene un índice que empieza en **0**. El último es `len(lista) - 1`. Los índices negativos cuentan desde el final: `-1` es el último."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "a = ['rojo', 'verde', 'azul']",
          "print(a[0])",
          "print(a[-1])"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "rojo",
          "azul"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Pedir un índice que no existe (p. ej. `a[5]`) provoca un `IndexError`. Recuerda que con 3 elementos los índices válidos son 0, 1 y 2."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Modificar listas"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`append(x)` añade al final, `insert(i, x)` inserta en una posición, `pop()` saca el último (o el de un índice) y `remove(x)` borra la primera aparición de `x`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "a = [1, 2, 3]",
          "a.append(4)",
          "a.pop(0)",
          "print(a)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "[2, 3, 4]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Recorrer y comprobar pertenencia"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Recorre una lista con `for`, y comprueba si contiene algo con `in`. `sorted(lista)` devuelve una copia ordenada."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "for x in [3, 1, 2]:",
          "    print(x)",
          "print(2 in [1, 2, 3])"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "3",
          "1",
          "2",
          "True"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Storing many values"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "A **list** is an ordered collection of values, written between square brackets and comma-separated. It can hold numbers, strings or anything, and grow or shrink."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "numbers = [10, 20, 30]",
          "print(numbers)",
          "print(len(numbers))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "[10, 20, 30]",
          "3"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Indices: access by position"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Each element has an index starting at **0**. The last is `len(list) - 1`. Negative indices count from the end: `-1` is the last."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "a = ['red', 'green', 'blue']",
          "print(a[0])",
          "print(a[-1])"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "red",
          "blue"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Asking for an index that doesn't exist (e.g. `a[5]`) raises an `IndexError`. With 3 elements, valid indices are 0, 1 and 2."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Modifying lists"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`append(x)` adds at the end, `insert(i, x)` inserts at a position, `pop()` removes the last (or one by index) and `remove(x)` deletes the first occurrence of `x`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "a = [1, 2, 3]",
          "a.append(4)",
          "a.pop(0)",
          "print(a)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "[2, 3, 4]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Iterating and membership"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Loop a list with `for`, and check if it contains something with `in`. `sorted(list)` returns a sorted copy."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "for x in [3, 1, 2]:",
          "    print(x)",
          "print(2 in [1, 2, 3])"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "3",
          "1",
          "2",
          "True"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m3l1e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `suma_lista(numeros)` que devuelva la suma de todos los números de la lista (sin usar `sum`).",
        "en": "Define `suma_lista(numeros)` returning the sum of all numbers in the list (without using `sum`)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def suma_lista(numeros):",
        "    total = 0",
        "    # recorre la lista",
        "    return total"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def suma_lista(numeros):",
        "    total = 0",
        "    for n in numeros:",
        "        total = total + n",
        "    return total"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Acumula en 'total' recorriendo con for.",
          "for n in numeros: total = total + n"
        ],
        "en": [
          "Accumulate in 'total' looping with for.",
          "for n in numeros: total = total + n"
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "name": "suma_lista",
          "function": "suma_lista",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  1,
                  2,
                  3
                ]
              ],
              "expected": 6
            },
            {
              "args": [
                []
              ],
              "expected": 0
            },
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  10,
                  -5
                ]
              ],
              "expected": 5
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m3l1e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `maximo(numeros)` que devuelva el mayor de la lista (sin usar `max`). La lista nunca estará vacía.",
        "en": "Define `maximo(numeros)` returning the largest in the list (without using `max`). The list is never empty."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def maximo(numeros):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def maximo(numeros):",
        "    mayor = numeros[0]",
        "    for n in numeros:",
        "        if n > mayor:",
        "            mayor = n",
        "    return mayor"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Empieza suponiendo que el mayor es el primer elemento.",
          "Recorre y actualiza si encuentras uno más grande."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Start assuming the largest is the first element.",
          "Loop and update if you find a bigger one."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "name": "maximo",
          "function": "maximo",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  3,
                  9,
                  2
                ]
              ],
              "expected": 9
            },
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  -1,
                  -7,
                  -3
                ]
              ],
              "expected": -1
            },
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  5
                ]
              ],
              "expected": 5
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m3l1e3",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `invertir(lista)` que devuelva una **nueva** lista con los elementos en orden inverso (no uses `reversed` ni `[::-1]`).",
        "en": "Define `invertir(lista)` returning a **new** list with the elements in reverse order (don't use `reversed` or `[::-1]`)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def invertir(lista):",
        "    resultado = []",
        "    return resultado"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def invertir(lista):",
        "    resultado = []",
        "    for x in lista:",
        "        resultado.insert(0, x)",
        "    return resultado"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "insert(0, x) coloca x al principio.",
          "Si recorres en orden e insertas al principio, queda invertida."
        ],
        "en": [
          "insert(0, x) puts x at the front.",
          "Iterating in order and inserting at the front reverses it."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "name": "invertir",
          "function": "invertir",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  1,
                  2,
                  3
                ]
              ],
              "expected": [
                3,
                2,
                1
              ]
            },
            {
              "args": [
                []
              ],
              "expected": []
            },
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  "a",
                  "b"
                ]
              ],
              "expected": [
                "b",
                "a"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}